{% schema %}
  {
    
    "name": "Section 2",
    "tag": "section",
    "class": "gps-635767739692090084 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/photobrickusa/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_ARTICLE&editorId=635767739457209060&sectionId=635767739692090084)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"ggpG-u0Nqvd_text","label":"ggpG-u0Nqvd_text","default":"It Does Not Matter If You Are Not a Builder"},{"type":"html","id":"ggEpU9i2_s9_text","label":"ggEpU9i2_s9_text","default":"<p>You might have someone in the family who loves building things.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You might also have someone who has never touched a building set in years.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That is okay.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A brick mosaic does not require everyone to have the same level of experience. The project can be approached slowly, and people can help with whatever part feels comfortable.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Some people will enjoy organizing pieces. Others will enjoy finding patterns. Some will want to build as quickly as possible.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The different personalities can actually make the activity more entertaining.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And because everyone is working toward the same final image, the focus stays on creating something together rather than competing over who is the best builder.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggHlOCE0sSP_text","label":"ggHlOCE0sSP_text","default":"A Holiday Project That Does Not End After One Day"},{"type":"html","id":"ggC2dUafp4Y_text","label":"ggC2dUafp4Y_text","default":"<p>Many holiday activities are over almost as quickly as they begin.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A board game gets packed away.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A movie finishes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Dinner is eaten.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A brick mosaic can be different because it can remain a project throughout the holiday break.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You can work on it after breakfast, return to it in the evening, or continue building the next day. There is no reason to rush through it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For larger mosaics, taking multiple sessions can even make the project more enjoyable because you always have something to come back to.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The progress itself becomes part of the fun.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggL9jopoVT__text","label":"ggL9jopoVT__text","default":"Watch the Picture Come Together"},{"type":"html","id":"ggwWFN8QXEq_text","label":"ggwWFN8QXEq_text","default":"<p>At the beginning, the mosaic may look like a collection of random colors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Then something changes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A recognizable shape appears.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A face begins to form.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A pet's features become visible.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A car starts taking shape.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Suddenly, everyone around the table understands what they are building.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That gradual transformation is one of the most enjoyable parts of a brick mosaic. The finished image does not simply appear. You watch it develop through your own work.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For a group activity, this creates a natural sense of excitement. Everyone can see the progress and look forward to the moment when the final section is complete.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggWy-DG8feH_text","label":"ggWy-DG8feH_text","default":"Choose an Image Everyone Will Enjoy"},{"type":"html","id":"ggT__xTvOd8_text","label":"ggT__xTvOd8_text","default":"<p>The image you choose can make the activity even more fun.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Instead of choosing something that only one person cares about, consider an image that represents the group.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It could be a holiday gathering from a previous year, a funny family photograph, a beloved pet, a group vacation, a favorite car, or even a picture from an ordinary day that everyone remembers.</p><p>You can also make the choice part of the activity.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Let everyone vote.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Give everyone a few options.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Ask the kids which picture they like best.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>There is no need to make the decision complicated. The goal is to choose something everyone will be excited to see come together.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggMrXFzkxMM_text","label":"ggMrXFzkxMM_text","default":"Make It a Family Challenge"},{"type":"html","id":"ggqgOfLrT5l_text","label":"ggqgOfLrT5l_text","default":"<p>If your family enjoys a little friendly competition, you can turn the building process into a lighthearted challenge.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Who can sort the colors fastest?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Who can find the missing piece?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Who can complete their section first?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You could even divide the mosaic into sections and let different people work on each area before connecting everything together.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The important thing is to keep it fun.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The project does not need winners or losers. Sometimes the best part is simply watching everyone become invested in the same goal.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>By the end, the finished mosaic is something the whole group can be proud of.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggjaAAx92ZQ_text","label":"ggjaAAx92ZQ_text","default":"A Great Activity for Different Ages"},{"type":"html","id":"ggyIM06Tfx3_text","label":"ggyIM06Tfx3_text","default":"<p>Holiday gatherings often bring together people who do not normally spend much time doing the same activities.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Young children have different interests from teenagers.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Teenagers have different interests from parents.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Grandparents may prefer something slower and more relaxed.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A brick mosaic can bridge those differences because everyone can participate at their own pace.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Younger builders can help sort pieces.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Older children can assemble sections.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Adults can work on more detailed areas.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Grandparents can participate while enjoying the conversation around the table.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It becomes less about finding an activity that perfectly matches everyone and more about finding something everyone can contribute to.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg5FMX6rEN6_text","label":"gg5FMX6rEN6_text","default":"The Finished Artwork Becomes Part of the Celebration"},{"type":"html","id":"gg_iVItzNDa_text","label":"gg_iVItzNDa_text","default":"<p>Eventually, the last piece goes into place.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Everyone steps back.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The scattered bricks are gone, and the image is finally complete.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That moment can feel surprisingly rewarding when several people have contributed to the project.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You can display the finished mosaic in the home, keep it as part of your seasonal decorations, or place it somewhere you can enjoy throughout the year.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The artwork becomes more than something you built during the holidays.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It becomes something that can remind you of the time everyone spent creating it together.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg7-Ji22-t__text","label":"gg7-Ji22-t__text","default":"A Creative Break From the Usual Holiday Routine"},{"type":"html","id":"ggCLhpVjdet_text","label":"ggCLhpVjdet_text","default":"<p>The holidays can become repetitive.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Eat.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Watch something.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Open presents.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Scroll through your phone.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Eat again.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>There is nothing wrong with those traditions, but adding a creative activity can give the day a different rhythm.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Building a mosaic gives everyone a reason to slow down and do something with their hands. It creates conversation without requiring anyone to come up with a complicated activity.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You simply sit together, pick up the pieces, and start building.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Sometimes that is all you need.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggb9PlQtYDp_text","label":"ggb9PlQtYDp_text","default":"Why Memobrick Works So Well for Group Building"},{"type":"html","id":"ggvkTVDQwYg_text","label":"ggvkTVDQwYg_text","default":"<p>A Memobrick mosaic combines an image people recognize with the hands on experience of building with individual bricks.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The design provides a clear goal, while the physical pieces make everyone part of the process.</p><p>Technology helps us create the design. People make sure we get it right.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That combination means the project is not only about the finished artwork. It is about giving people something they can actually participate in.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Whether the group is building a family photo, a pet portrait, a vehicle, a holiday scene, or another image they enjoy, the experience can be adapted to the people around the table.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggK04FUTDvt_text","label":"ggK04FUTDvt_text","default":"Make This Holiday About More Than Staying Busy"},{"type":"html","id":"gg8HXjTwCHb_text","label":"gg8HXjTwCHb_text","default":"<p>A good holiday activity does not need complicated rules, expensive equipment, or hours of preparation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Sometimes the best activities are the ones that give everyone something to do while naturally creating opportunities to talk and spend time together.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A brick mosaic does exactly that.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Start with an image everyone enjoys.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Spread the pieces across the table.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Let everyone choose a section.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Build together.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Laugh when someone puts a piece in the wrong place.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Celebrate when the image finally becomes recognizable.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And when the final piece is added, you have something physical to show for the time you spent together.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggSIFSmb5qj_text","label":"ggSIFSmb5qj_text","default":"Reviews from Happy Customers"},{"type":"html","id":"ggYtRXjDI8D_text","label":"ggYtRXjDI8D_text","default":"<p>So easy to understand and a nice relaxing project for my free time. Can't wait to do another one!</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggKXSFfWFbl_text","label":"ggKXSFfWFbl_text","default":"<p>-Aaryn C.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggaCii03Ne4_childItem_0","label":"ggaCii03Ne4_childItem_0","default":"<p>Verified Customer</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggkn9YigrVF_text","label":"ggkn9YigrVF_text","default":"<p>\"I love these memo bricks! I ordered a smaller size, but when they emailed the mockup they showed me the difference of what it would look like compared to the bigger size. I was offered to upgrade\"</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggymABV5hia_text","label":"ggymABV5hia_text","default":"<p>-Kelsey M.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggN3UdyYrm4_childItem_0","label":"ggN3UdyYrm4_childItem_0","default":"<p>Verified Customer</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg0V4YtCsoB_text","label":"gg0V4YtCsoB_text","default":"<p>&nbsp;\"I split the photo in half so I could get 2 of the 60x20 so I could fill my wall more and its turned out AMAZING!\"</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg5kkV4D4v9_text","label":"gg5kkV4D4v9_text","default":"<p>-Candice L.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggGMFheTViq_childItem_0","label":"ggGMFheTViq_childItem_0","default":"<p>Verified Customer</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggnO3VYmVUW_text","label":"ggnO3VYmVUW_text","default":"<p>\"Excellent customer service! The design team did an excellent job and we are so pleased to have a precious family picture transformed into such a cool art form.\"</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg20jQGtbrE_text","label":"gg20jQGtbrE_text","default":"<p>-Aaron M.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggVF_j4u8Y__childItem_0","label":"ggVF_j4u8Y__childItem_0","default":"<p>Verified Customer</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggI2x3WWtdi_text","label":"ggI2x3WWtdi_text","default":"<p>The best holiday activities are not always the loudest or most complicated.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Sometimes they are the ones that bring everyone to the same table.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>A brick mosaic gives children something to build, adults something creative to work on, and everyone a reason to spend a little more time together.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Start with a picture.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Pass around the pieces.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Build a section.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Then build another.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Before long, the table is full of progress and the image is beginning to appear.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And when the final brick is placed, you will have more than a finished mosaic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You will have something everyone helped create.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>This holiday, build something together.</strong></p>"}],
